    "name":  "Corporo-venous occlusive erectile dysfunction",
    "module":  "male-genital",
    "category":  "disease",
    "description":  "Corporo-venous occlusive erectile dysfunction (venous leak ED) is a form of organic erectile dysfunction caused by failure of the veno-occlusive mechanism of the corpora cavernosa. During normal erection, sinusoidal smooth muscle relaxation expands the corpora, compressing the emissary veins and preventing venous outflow. In venous leak, structural changes (Peyronie\u0027s disease, fibrosis, aging) prevent adequate veno-occlusion, so the erection cannot be maintained despite adequate arterial inflow. It is diagnosed by colour duplex Doppler ultrasound showing abnormally high end-diastolic velocity after intracavernosal injection.",
